# Chroma library, modern Earth: what the Protection sphere's events bring into a life (Library thread, 2026-10-09,
# "v22" update stage 4, item 15 phase 3: a moment for each sphere event that touches the character). Design:
# chroma-ideas/spheres-implementation.md sections 2, 4 "Library" and 5; data chroma-ideas/spheres-data/prot.json (each
# event's trigger, on_character and wording.modern; the faces and pairs). Fields: build.py (WORLD_SIT, WORLD_OPT and the
# spheres' fields, world-fields.md 2026-10-09).
#
# Every moment here is an event moment: a life event with per_year all 0 (it exists only with the world and the
# sph_events switch on), no drivers, sphere: prot and sphere_event: <key>. The Engine fires each on its event for the
# people its selector names; the '# world:' line above each names the event key, the selector and the share of selected
# people who get the moment (estimate). Every option carries sphere: the face it acts in (prot.X for a one-colour option,
# the pair face in wheel order for a pair option).
#
# Which events: every prot event whose epochs include modern and that has on_character, 21 in all, less one the world
# already brings: call_up (fired with the world's 'war begins') is 'the call to serve' (earth-world-civic.lib), so it is
# skipped. crime_wave, disaster_strikes and peace_made also ride on world events (section 5), but earth.py has no moment
# for them as a town's event: 'robbed or attacked in the street' is one's own robbery, 'a disaster in the next town' is a
# read event of a town nearby, 'the town builds itself back' is the recovery, and no moment marks a war's end; so they
# are written here. 20 moments.
#
# Layout: each is a life event with five one-colour options and one half of a pair set; the twelve halves D1a to D6b
# are each used once or twice (both halves of every D), picked so the set holds the pair the event's data names where
# it can (raid_foiled UB, watch_founded WU, heavy_hand and brave_stand RW, veterans_home and civil_war BG ...).
# Evenness: in every moment each colour's one-colour chance plus half its two pairs' chances is the same sum, so every
# colour has the same mean chance in each moment and so in every stage. No flags.
#
# Safety: war, crime and disaster are told indirectly and never graphically; no option kills or uses a weapon on anyone;
# no child is harmed (the moments open at 14); nothing sexual. No real place, war, force, brand or year.
#
# share: and once: on every moment (2026-10-10, Engine phase 3c): the engine draws at birth who can ever meet the
# moment (share:), and they meet it at most once (once: yes). Shares are the '# world:' share times .5, so the 157
# moments together come to about 13 a life at the fitted event rates (Engine table chroma-engine/notes/sphev-per-moment.tsv:
# 92 a life before). The '# world:' line keeps the share of the people an event reaches, as written.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- raid_foiled (pairs D1b)

# world: sphere event raid_foiled, selector place, share .05
== the van that keeps circling
tier: life event
stages: juvenile+
age: 14-90
sphere: prot
sphere_event: raid_foiled
share: 0.03
once: yes
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
times: World event: raid_foiled (sphere prot). The lookouts see them coming: a planned theft or robbery in the place is noticed and reported in time; about 1 in 20 people there are the ones who notice or pass on the warning (share .05, estimate); most people meet it once in a life or never (estimate)
likelier: a street where people know each other's cars, a shop or depot that handles cash, a watch or a guard that answers calls
rarer: a busy anonymous centre, a street where nobody reports anything
gap: 10-30
tone: joy
life: work, community
horizon: week
roles: colleague, boss, neighbours, friend
earth: for three days running the same van has circled the depot at closing time, slowing by the gate
scene: For three evenings running the same van has crept past the depot at closing time, slowing by the gate just as the takings go out. Nobody else seems to have noticed.
scene W: There is a number to ring for exactly this. {N} has never rung it, and feels foolish even thinking of it.
scene U: {N} has started writing down the times: ten past six, twelve past, eight past. The van comes when the cash bags leave, every time.
scene B: Whoever stops a robbery before it happens is owed something. {N} wonders who would be grateful enough to say so.
scene R: {Ns} pulse jumps every time the van turns the corner. Part of {N} wants to walk straight up and knock on the window.
scene G: {N} knows every car on this street and whose it is. This one belongs to nobody here.
- W | ring the police and report the van, its plate and the times | v: security, conformity | lever: voice | pushes: institution police | sphere: prot.W | chance: 75
- U | keep a log of the van's times for a week before saying anything | v: self-direction, security | sphere: prot.U | chance: 68
- B | take what you saw to the depot's owner, and make sure they know who spotted it | v: achievement, power | sphere: prot.B | chance: 75
- R | walk over and ask the driver straight out what they are waiting for | v: stimulation, self-direction | mark: took a wild risk | sphere: prot.R | chance: 66
- G | tell the neighbours and the other shops on the street to keep an eye out | v: benevolence, security | sphere: prot.G | chance: 70
- RG | stay late with two neighbours and stand by the gate when the bags go out | v: benevolence, stimulation | lever: loyalty | sphere: prot.RG | chance: 70
- UB | have a quiet word with the guard firm that collects the takings | v: security, achievement | sphere: prot.UB | chance: 66
- UR | photograph the van's plate as it passes, and send it in that night | v: stimulation, security | tech: phone | sphere: prot.UR | chance: 74
- WB | ask the manager to change the collection time and the route, and log it | v: security, conformity | sphere: prot.WB | chance: 60
- WG | ring the police, then knock on every door on the street that evening | v: benevolence, conformity | sphere: prot.GW | chance: 66
works: The van stops coming. Weeks later {N} hears the police found its plates on a car in another town.
works: Nothing happens, which is the whole point, and the owner shakes {Ns} hand at the door.
fails: Nobody takes {N} seriously, and the van goes on circling as if nothing had been said.
fails: The van turns out to be a lost delivery driver three days in a row, and {N} hears about it for months.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- siege (pairs D3b)

# world: sphere event siege, selector place, share .8
== the city is surrounded
tier: life event
stages: juvenile+
age: 14-95
sphere: prot
sphere_event: siege
share: 0.41
once: yes
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
times: World event: siege (sphere prot). A town cut off by a hostile force for weeks or months comes only with a war and is very rare in a stable state; inside it almost everyone lives through it as a moment of their own (share .8, estimate); far fewer than 1 in 100 lives in modern Earth meet one (estimate)
likelier: a war on the border, a town with walls of river or hills that can be closed, thin stores
rarer: a stable state at peace, a town with open roads in every direction
gap: 20-60
tone: trouble
life: home, community
horizon: months
roles: parent, sibling, neighbours, friend
earth: the city is surrounded: power and water fail by turns, the shops are bare, and neighbours cook together in the stairwell
scene: The roads out of {place} have been closed for five weeks. The power comes on for two hours a day, the water for one, and the whole stairwell cooks on a single gas ring on the landing.
scene W: The council has drawn up a ration list, a name and a share for every flat. {N} thinks it only works if everyone keeps to it.
scene U: {N} has worked out how long the stores in the building will last at this rate: nineteen days, perhaps twenty-two.
scene B: A tin of milk powder now buys a week of someone's labour. {N} knows who on the landing still has a full cupboard.
scene R: Sitting in the dark and waiting is the hardest part. {N} would rather be out doing anything at all.
scene G: {Ns} family has lived in this building for three generations. Whatever happens, they go through it together, here.
- W | put your stores on the ration list and take only your share | v: universalism, conformity | mark: kept your word | lever: loyalty | pushes: place | sphere: prot.W | chance: 68
- U | rig a rain catcher and a filter on the roof for the whole building | v: self-direction, benevolence | mark: learned a skill | sphere: prot.U | chance: 65
- B | trade the spare batteries you put by for food and favours | v: power, security | sphere: prot.B | chance: 78
- R | join the crews that carry water to the defenders at the edge of town | v: stimulation, benevolence | mark: took a wild risk | lever: loyalty | sphere: prot.R | chance: 73
- G | keep the family in the flat, and share only with the neighbours you know | v: security, tradition | sphere: prot.G | chance: 62
- BR | make the night runs for supplies through the back streets, for a share | v: stimulation, power | mark: took a wild risk | sphere: prot.BR | chance: 50
- UG | plant beans and herbs in every window box and in the courtyard | v: security, self-direction | sphere: prot.GU | chance: 66
- UR | patch up the old generator so the stairwell has light at night | v: achievement, benevolence | sphere: prot.UR | chance: 64
- WB | get the council to pay the building's volunteers in food, and keep the books | v: security, achievement | pushes: place | sphere: prot.WB | chance: 54
- WG | cook for the whole stairwell every night from what everyone brings | v: benevolence, tradition | mark: helped someone in need | sphere: prot.GW | chance: 70
works: The roads open in the spring, and the stairwell that cooked together stays friends for good.
works: {N} comes through it thinner and steadier, and so do the people {N} kept close.
fails: The weeks drag into months, and {N} learns what hunger does to a temper.
fails: A quarrel over food splits the landing, and some doors stay shut long after the roads open.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- peace_made (pairs D2b)

# world: sphere event peace_made, selector all, share .3
== the ceasefire holds
tier: life event
stages: juvenile+
age: 14-100
sphere: prot
sphere_event: peace_made
share: 0.15
once: yes
who: sibling
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
times: World event: peace_made (sphere prot), with the world's 'war ends'. It comes only after a war; in a country that was at war nearly everyone feels the peace, and about 3 in 10 meet it as a moment of their own: someone close home, the border open, prices easing (share .3, estimate)
likelier: someone close who served, a border town, a long war
rarer: a war fought far away by a professional army
gap: 15-60
tone: joy
life: home, community
horizon: months
roles: sibling, parent, friend, neighbours
earth: the ceasefire holds, the treaty is signed, and the reservists start coming home
scene: The ceasefire held, and this morning the treaty was signed. The trains are full of reservists coming home, the border crossing opens on Monday, and {sibling} has sent a message: the evening train.
scene W: A treaty is a promise kept on both sides. {N} reads its terms in full and hopes both sides mean them.
scene U: {N} wonders what the peace will change: the prices, the jobs, the border, and who will take the credit.
scene B: When the border opens, trade opens with it. {N} is already thinking about what could cross it.
scene R: {N} wants to be on the platform when the train comes in, and to cheer until {Ns} voice goes.
scene G: There will be a full table again at last, with every chair taken.
- W | go to the service for the ones who did not come back | v: tradition, conformity | lever: loyalty | sphere: prot.W | chance: 79
- U | read the treaty through and work out what it means for the town | v: self-direction, universalism | mark: learned a skill | sphere: prot.U | chance: 76
- B | be first across the reopened border with goods the other side has gone without | v: achievement, power | mark: took a wild risk | sphere: prot.B | chance: 75
- R | meet the evening train with a crowd of friends and a great deal of noise | v: hedonism, stimulation | sphere: prot.R | chance: 80
- G | cook the homecoming meal and set every place at the table | v: tradition, benevolence | sphere: prot.G | chance: 74
- RG | throw a street party for everyone who came home, and their families | v: hedonism, benevolence | mark: made a friend | sphere: prot.RG | chance: 66
- UB | find the returning reservists work, for a fee from the firms that hire them | v: achievement, power | sphere: prot.UB | chance: 62
- UG | give the one who came home time and quiet, and listen when they want to talk | v: benevolence | sphere: prot.GU | chance: 66
- WB | help run the council's desk that finds each returning reservist a post | v: security, achievement | pushes: place | sphere: prot.WB | chance: 68
- WR | speak at the town meeting for keeping the peace when the hard voices start | v: universalism, benevolence | lever: voice | pushes: state | sphere: prot.RW | chance: 54
works: {sibling} steps off the train, thinner and grinning, and the evening is one {N} keeps for life.
works: Prices ease by summer, the border stays open, and the town breathes out.
fails: The peace holds, but the one who came home is quieter than before, and the house feels it.
fails: The celebrations sour into an argument over who won what, and {N} goes home early.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- veterans_home (pairs D1a)

# world: sphere event veterans_home, selector place, share .15
== home from service for good
tier: life event
stages: juvenile+
age: 14-95
sphere: prot
sphere_event: veterans_home
share: 0.08
once: yes
who: friend
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
times: World event: veterans_home (sphere prot). When a war ends after many served, the fighters come home; about 15 in 100 people in the place have a friend or a sibling among them and meet it as a moment (share .15, estimate); a person meets it once in a life or never (estimate)
likelier: a long war, a town that sent many, a friend or sibling who served
rarer: a short war, a professional army drawn from far away
gap: 15-60
tone: mixed
life: ties, home
horizon: years
roles: friend, sibling, parent
earth: a close friend is home from service for good: a study grant, a long wait at the clinic, and long silences
scene: {friend} is home from service for good, with a study grant, a clinic appointment four months away, and a way of going quiet in the middle of a sentence.
scene W: {friend} served because the country asked. {N} thinks the least the town owes is a proper welcome and a fair way back.
scene U: {N} has read about what long service does to sleep and temper, and watches {friend} more closely than {friend} would like.
scene B: The grant is good money if it is used well. {N} wonders whether {friend} knows what it can buy.
scene R: {N} wants the old {friend} back: the laughing one, the one who started things. Maybe one good night out will do it.
scene G: {friend} has a seat at {Ns} table whenever they want it, for as long as they want it.
- W | go with them to the veterans' office and sort out every form they are owed | v: benevolence, conformity | sphere: prot.W | chance: 69
- U | find out which courses the study grant pays for, and help them choose | v: benevolence, self-direction | sphere: prot.U | chance: 66
- B | get them taken on at a guard firm where a soldier's skills pay well | v: achievement, security | sphere: prot.B | chance: 74
- R | take them out to the old places with the old crowd, just like before | v: hedonism, stimulation | sphere: prot.R | chance: 73
- G | keep a place at the table for them every Sunday, and ask nothing | v: benevolence, tradition | sphere: prot.G | chance: 72
- BG | help them put the grant into a small trade of their own near home | v: security, achievement | sphere: prot.BG | chance: 56
- BR | go into business with them: a removals van, two strong backs and no boss | v: self-direction, achievement | sphere: prot.BR | chance: 60
- UG | walk the hills with them on Saturdays, and let them talk or not | v: benevolence | sphere: prot.GU | chance: 64
- WR | stand up for them at the clinic until they are seen sooner | v: benevolence, universalism | lever: voice | pushes: institution hospital | sphere: prot.RW | chance: 58
- WU | join the veterans' group at the hall and help run its evenings | v: benevolence, conformity | lever: loyalty | sphere: prot.WU | chance: 68
works: Slowly {friend} comes back into the world, and {N} is one of the reasons why.
works: A year on, {friend} is studying, laughing again, and teasing {N} about all the fuss.
fails: {friend} drifts from the old crowd, and from {N} too, and nothing seems to reach them.
fails: Whatever {N} tries that year is the wrong thing, and the friendship goes quiet for a long time.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- safe_passage (pairs D4b)

# world: sphere event safe_passage, selector place, share .2
== a night guard for the main street
tier: life event
stages: juvenile+
age: 16-90
sphere: prot
sphere_event: safe_passage
share: 0.1
once: yes
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
times: World event: safe_passage (sphere prot). The road is made safe: the traders of a street or a quarter pay together for a guard; about 1 in 5 people in the place work or live on the guarded street and meet it as a moment (share .2, estimate)
likelier: a winter of break-ins, a high street of small shops, traders who already meet
rarer: a street of chain stores with their own guards, a quarter with no shops
gap: 10-30
tone: joy
life: work, community, money
horizon: months
roles: neighbours, boss, colleague, friend
earth: after a winter of break-ins, the shopkeepers on the main street agree to share the cost of a night guard
scene: After a winter of break-ins, the shopkeepers on the main street meet in the back of the bakery and agree to share the cost of a night guard. They need someone to run it, everyone to pay in, and someone to walk it.
scene W: A guard for the street should be a guard for every shop, whether it paid the most or the least. {N} says so.
scene U: {N} has the dates and times of every break-in this winter, and a fair idea which hours the guard should walk.
scene B: A night guard is a wage. A firm of guards is a living. {N} has been thinking about that for a while.
scene R: {N} would walk the street at night for nothing, just for the feel of it, and is half tempted to say so.
scene G: These are {Ns} neighbours. If the street is to be kept, it should be kept by people who live on it.
- W | draw up one fair rule for what each shop pays and what the guard covers | v: universalism, conformity | sphere: prot.W | chance: 72
- U | map the winter's break-ins and plan the guard's rounds from them | v: self-direction, achievement | mark: learned a skill | sphere: prot.U | chance: 70
- B | bid for the job at a proper price, and run it as a business | v: achievement, power | lever: found | sphere: prot.B | chance: 76
- R | take the night shift yourself and walk the street until dawn | v: stimulation, benevolence | lever: loyalty | sphere: prot.R | chance: 77
- G | pay your share and keep a light on in your window at night | v: security, benevolence | lever: fund | sphere: prot.G | chance: 69
- BR | start a small guard crew of your own with two friends and a van | v: achievement, stimulation | lever: found | sphere: prot.BR | chance: 56
- UB | get a cheaper rate from the big guard firm by sharing it with the next street | v: achievement, security | sphere: prot.UB | chance: 64
- UG | set up a phone tree between the guard and the flats above the shops | v: security, benevolence | tech: phone | sphere: prot.GU | chance: 68
- WG | collect the money door to door and keep the book of who has paid | v: conformity, benevolence | lever: lead | sphere: prot.GW | chance: 66
- WR | speak up for the corner shop that cannot pay, and cover its share | v: benevolence, universalism | lever: voice | sphere: prot.RW | chance: 62
works: The break-ins stop, and by summer two empty shops on the street have opened again.
works: The street feels like a street again at night, and {N} had a hand in it.
fails: Half the shops stop paying by the second month, and the guard goes with the money.
fails: The guard keeps the main street safe, and the break-ins simply move round the corner.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- new_arms (pairs D5a)

# world: sphere event new_arms, selector staff, share .5
== the new radios and phone maps
tier: life event
stages: young_adult adult mature
age: 18-67
sphere: prot
sphere_event: new_arms
share: 0.25
once: yes
at: police
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
times: World event: new_arms (sphere prot). New kit and new drill reach the watch and the volunteer crews; about half of the staff of a police station or a rescue crew meet the change as a moment of their own (share .5, estimate); a long career sees two or three such changes (estimate)
likelier: a station with new money, a young force, a town where volunteer crews work beside the police
rarer: a poor force that keeps the old kit, a desk post far from the patrols
gap: 8-20
tone: mixed
life: work
horizon: months
roles: colleague, boss, mentor
earth: cheap radios and phone maps reach every patrol and volunteer crew, and the old ways of working are worth less overnight
scene: The new radios and phone maps came into the station on Monday. Every patrol now sees every other on one screen, and the sergeant says the old ways of working are finished.
scene W: The new kit comes with a new drill, and the drill will be the same for everyone. {N} likes that.
scene U: {N} has already found three things the maps get wrong, and two things they could do that nobody has tried.
scene B: The officers who master the new kit first will be the ones who are promoted. {N} means to be one of them.
scene R: {N} made a name by knowing the streets by heart and getting there first. Now a screen does it.
scene G: The old hands knew every alley and every family. {N} wonders whether a map can know a street like that.
- W | do the training course properly and pass the new drill first time | v: conformity, achievement | mark: learned a skill | lever: loyalty | pushes: institution police | sphere: prot.W | chance: 59
- U | test the maps on your own beat and write up where they go wrong | v: self-direction, achievement | lever: voice | pushes: institution police | sphere: prot.U | chance: 66
- B | ask for the new specialist post, and the pay that comes with it | v: achievement, power | sphere: prot.B | chance: 64
- R | keep your own way of working, and trust your feet over the screen | v: self-direction, stimulation | lever: neglect | sphere: prot.R | chance: 64
- G | teach the volunteer crews in your patch to use the new kit | v: benevolence | sphere: prot.G | chance: 59
- BG | train the neighbours' watch on the radios, for a modest fee | v: achievement, benevolence | sphere: prot.BG | chance: 64
- UB | sell the station a better way to use the maps, and take the credit | v: achievement, power | sphere: prot.UB | chance: 60
- UR | build a faster call-out plan with the new kit, and try it on the night shift | v: stimulation, achievement | sphere: prot.UR | chance: 60
- WG | pair each new recruit with an old hand who knows the streets | v: tradition, benevolence | lever: lead | sphere: prot.GW | chance: 70
- WR | take the first night out with the new kit, and show the doubters it works | v: stimulation, conformity | sphere: prot.RW | chance: 64
works: Within a season {N} is the one the others ask about the new kit.
works: The new kit and the old knowledge turn out to need each other, and {N} has both.
fails: The new system drops out on the busiest night of the year, and {N} takes the blame.
fails: {N} falls behind the younger ones on the screens, and is quietly moved to a desk.

