- U | ring the police quietly, and give them the stop and a description | v: security | sphere: prot.U | chance: 69
- B | step up beside the driver and talk the man down, calm and firm | v: power, benevolence | mark: took a wild risk | sphere: prot.B | chance: 68
- R | stand up and tell him, loudly, to sit down | v: stimulation, benevolence | mark: took a wild risk | sphere: prot.R | chance: 74
- G | move the old man and the others to the back, away from the trouble | v: benevolence, security | mark: helped someone in need | sphere: prot.G | chance: 69
- BG | keep your seat by the door, and quietly shield the passengers behind it | v: security, benevolence | sphere: prot.BG | chance: 64
- UB | ask the man what he wants, and get him off at the next stop | v: power, security | sphere: prot.UB | chance: 60
- UR | film it on your phone and call out that the police can already see it | v: stimulation, security | tech: phone | sphere: prot.UR | chance: 62
- WG | get the passengers on their feet together behind the driver | v: benevolence, universalism | sphere: prot.GW | chance: 58
- WR | stand between the man and the driver's door until the police come | v: benevolence, universalism | mark: took a wild risk | sphere: prot.RW | chance: 50
works: The man gets off at the next stop, the bus cheers, and the driver thanks {N} at the depot.
works: The local paper runs a picture of the bus, and {Ns} friends will not stop talking about it.
fails: It is over in a minute, and {N} goes home shaking, wishing for a braver minute.
fails: The man gets away, the police take statements, and {N} replays it for weeks.

